      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Elias's monologue should scream that these AI-run systems are a betrayal of the American soul, replacing human judgment with cold, unfeeling algorithms that serve only corporate profit. He must argue that tearing down these institutions isn't just rebellion, but the only way to reclaim our democracy from the grip of faceless tech giants who have already stolen our freedom. This isn't about fear; it's about the desperate, righteous necessity of smashing the machine to let real people breathe again.",
